course: dictionary
lesson: 14072
title: Big words: maximal
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Maximal is a formal word. It means as big or as great as possible, the largest. «She put in maximal effort to finish the race.» Here it means she tried as hard as she could.
explain: In maths, maximal means the greatest in a set. In «3, 8, 5, 1», the maximal value is 8, because no number in the set is bigger.
explain: Most people say maximum or the most instead. Maximal means the same thing, but you will meet it in books, tests and science. When you see it, ask: what is the biggest possible here?
fact: Maximal means as big or as great as possible.
fact: «Maximal» means the same as «maximum» and «the most».
fact: In maths, a maximal value is the greatest number in a set.
fact: Phrases you may see: «maximal effort» means the hardest you can try; «maximal value» means the biggest value.
exercise: «She ran with maximal effort to win the race.» What does maximal mean here? | Very slowly | *As great as possible | Quietly | Not at all
exercise: In the set 3, 8, 5, 1, which number is the maximal value? | 1 | *8 | 5 | 3
exercise: Pupils often say maximum or the most. Which formal word means the same? | Minimal | Tiny | Average | *Maximal
test: «The bridge can carry a maximal load of ten tonnes.» What does maximal load mean? | The smallest load | A load of about half | A load with no weight at all | *The largest load possible
test: In the set 12, 40, 7, 25, which number is the maximal value? | 7 | *40 | 25 | 12
exam: Which phrase uses maximal correctly? | maximal blue | maximal sleepy | maximal yesterday | *maximal effort
